auditcore_dummybundle 0.1.0 — attribution and authorization

New implementation in auditcore. No code was copied from other repositories.

The calculation rules (claims bound to the approved amount, receipts bound to
their claim, payment applications as sums of claims, accounts reconciled to
the final payment application) follow the proposal of 2026-10-13 and the
generator of a training course on accounts; its scenario, cases, solutions,
catalogues and word lists are not included.

The column headers of the templates V5 and V6 reproduce Annex XXIII and
Annex XXIV of Regulation (EU) 2021/1060 (OJ L 231, 30.6.2021, German
version, retrieved on 2026-10-13 from the Publications Office of the
European Union). They remain content of the European Union.

Company names, city names, postal codes, first and last names and purpose
phrases are read from the catalogues of auditcore_dummygenerator (MIT) at run
time. The company names are generic sample names; any resemblance to existing
companies is coincidental and not intended.

Release of the template profiles: on 2026-10-13 the rights holder released
the eleven template profiles of this package (V0 to V9 and N1, version
0.1.0), each in the version of its content hash. The release does not cover
the profiles of auditcore_dummygenerator (unchanged: NOT_GRANTED) nor texts
of third parties: the table headers of Annex XXIII and Annex XXIV are Union
law.

On 2026-09-22 the rights holder decided: "die Bibliotheken sollen MIT sein,
die anderen Repos nicht; die Bibliotheken kommen nach auditcore".
Status: USER_AUTHORIZED_MIT for this library.

The library generates practice data; it does not decide. Shares, rates and
value limits are parameters of the caller. Every output is marked
SYNTHETISCH.
